    "body":  "Closes no implementation Issue. Design review for [Issue #40](https://github.com/odango-chan/ca-agent-next/issues/40), layered **on top of PR #44** (head/base: `docs/issue-40-casl-160-capability-design-review` -\u003e `docs/issue-43-sr004-importer-readiness-20261126`). After #44 is merged into `docs/restore-original-designs-20261125`, retarget this PR to that restored base and rerun its exact-Head checks. Do **not** merge before independent review / final CI. This PR does not modify `main`.\n\n## Review conclusion / status\nAll affected central design documents are **待评审 / READY FOR DESIGN REVIEW**, not **implementation READY**. CA-SL **1.6.0 only** is the future *release target*, not an already released language or product. Nothing in this PR approves implementation, publishes a language/runtime artifact, or declares a new product/E2E PASS.\n\n## Single-version architecture: no compatibility\n- **Do not create `v1alpha6`**. CA-SL **1.6.0** is the sole new authoring/Compiler/Runtime/Studio/Bundle target. Exact machine `languageTarget` remains to be frozen by ca-skills/Compiler Owners; do not invent it.\n- Capability ID is the only Skill-facing public operation reference; Capability ↔ public Callable must be 1:1 *both directions*. Operation/Observation are Node stages, not extra Operation IDs. Compiler links a unique checked Capability→Callable binding and Runtime internally enforces exact Callable Scope, kind, Effect and Schema. Model/Skill/Studio do not select Callable IDs.\n- The new Compiler Parser/Check/Build/Verify/BuildRequest/BuildResult/Artifact, Agent Importer/Runtime, Studio and new Skill Bundle **do not support any old CA-SL language, Build DTO, Artifact, Bundle, alias, fallback, version-negotiation, migration, or mixed Catalog**. Historical v1alpha5 bytes/Golden/Release remain readonly audits, not new inputs; old Skill sources require author re-writing and new Build/Verify/release.\n- Owner cardinality audit from historical package: 24 capabilities / 25 Callable memberships, split establishment and release events by differing Schema/Evidence; MAS.RECONCILE is internal-only, Receipt Query remains a normal READ. Provider historical 2 capabilities / 11 READ Callables to be re-published as 2 public Callables with closed contextKind/resourceKind selectors routing 8+3 internal backendOperationIds.\n\n## Scope of this review\n- **New** [SR-029](https://github.com/odango-chan/ca-agent-next/blob/docs/issue-40-casl-160-capability-design-review/docs/SR/SR-029-Capability-first-Skill作者接口与Callable一对一绑定.md) v0.2.3, [IR-008](https://github.com/odango-chan/ca-agent-next/blob/docs/issue-40-casl-160-capability-design-review/docs/IR/IR%20总登记册.md), review-only design ACs (independent GitHub approval not yet given).\n- System architecture v0.4.5, EC01 CA-SL/Skill authoring architecture v0.1.2, language version spec v0.2.5.\n- Tool/Capability terminology, public ownership contracts, F03 Plugin/F03.05 Provider, F04 Runtime Action, F06 OpenAMSM MAS Create/Modify/Release design; EC02 Compiler v0.2.9; F09 Studio v0.3.10.\n- F02 v0.2.17, F08 v0.3.12 and skill format v0.1.8 stage 1.6.0-only designs as pending review.\n- SR-004 v0.2.7 / SR-013 v0.2.12 / SR-027 v0.1.6: **DRAFT, design pending review, implementation NOT_READY**, pending 1.6.0 language/Owner/Provider Package contract, Compiler new API/Binding, formal Bundle.\n- SR index/status/feature tree/central doc index/cross-repo audit/Agent.md synchronized. **8 IR; 28 SR = 4 VERIFIED, 1 IMPLEMENTED, 23 DRAFT** (SR-029 among DRAFT). Real Git tree **158 Markdown files**, including docs 155, two root files, one Echo example README. Existing SR-002/003/024 VERIFIED records unaffected.\n- Only central Markdown documents changed, no product implementation or changes to ca-skills, Compiler, env-openamsm, ca-client-tools, Studio or `main`.\n\n## Acceptance and evidence\n- Check all changed Markdown relative links (path and important anchors), duplicate section numbers, fence pairs, revision-table column consistency, latest version/revision row.\n- Verify no accidental assertion that new Compiler API, 1.6.0 language, Package, Bundle, Studio or MAS E2E is already released/implemented/PASS.\n- Historic Owner/Provider cardinality counts from pinned sources are **design evidence only**; 1.6.0 code/Release/Golden/E2E **NOT_RUN**.\n- **Final PR #45 Head `3c7c48383c52504a4861900bc1f8b731442f16c2`**: [Review Context Run #45830653094](https://github.com/odango-chan/ca-agent-next/actions/runs/45830653094) **SUCCESS**; all 80 review-context unit tests PASS, formal document scope validation PASS, and the generated review context was accepted. An earlier Head CI #45830200430 failed on three formal-document header declarations; those three headers were corrected, followed by the final-success CI above. No runtime product tests were triggered by this documentation-only PR.\n- Review-ready static checks: 25 changed Markdown docs, latest revision rows and column counts checked, code fences closed, no duplicate top-level numbered sections, and relative file targets resolved in audited docs. Formal document headers now use the exact review_scope inheritance declaration. Historical source docs remain archives, not new active schema.\n- No independent Github APPROVE is claimed (author/connected GitHub identity is the same). The PR is **ready for independent design review**, not merged, and is not implementation READY.\n",
